Welcome to Redblue v0.2.0 - tree-walking interpreter
Type ':help' for commands, ':quit' to exit
TAB completes, Up arrow walks back through history, !! repeats the last line

>>> Redblue tutorial — type each snippet, or ask for a hint with :hint

  1. A value, and a name for it
     Redblue reads as English. `set x to 5` gives 5 the name x.
     > set name to "World"
     > say name

  2. Arithmetic
     Numbers do what numbers do. Parentheses group, as they always do.
     > set x to (10 + 5) * 2
     > say x

  3. A condition
     `if … then … else … end` chooses between two paths.
     > set age to 30
     > if age is greater than 18 then
     >     say "Adult"
     > else
     >     say "Minor"
     > end

  4. A loop
     Blocks end with `end`. Everything indented inside them runs once per turn.
     > repeat 3 times
     >     say "Hello!"
     > end

  5. A function
     `to name(args) … end` defines one. Its body is what the name does.
     > to greet(who)
